{
  "raw": {
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#aircraft-mechanic": {
      "title": "Aircraft Mechanic",
      "description": "Aircraft Mechanic. Department: Flight School. Full-time Staff. Posted 2026-04-13. The University of Mount Olive has an immediate opening for an Aircraft Mechanic. Responsibilities include: • Perform daily, pre-flight, and special inspections for damage, corrosion, or wear. Includes aircraft cleaning, waxing and care of paint and Interior • Demonstrate strong technical expertise in aircraft systems and safety compliance • Troubleshoot mechanical and electrical problems using diagnostic tools and flight data. • Repair or replace faulty parts in engines, landing gear, hydraulics, brakes, and control systems • Service engines, hydraulic systems, deicers, and other components • Maintain detailed records of all maintenance, inspections, and repairs • Adhere strictly to FAA and manufacturer safety guidelines • Ability to work with the Federal Aviation Administration to keep the FAA Part 141 in compliance • Other duties may be assigned by the supervisor as required to meet the needs and growth of the position Minimum Qualifications: Valid FAA Airframe & Powerplant (A&P) License required, High school diploma or equivalent, Associate’s degree in Aviation Maintenance preferred. The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship. To Apply: Submit a cover letter, resume, and a list of three professional references by email to amiranda@umo.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. The University of Mount Olive is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes applicants from underrepresented groups. To learn more about the University of Mount Olive, please visit: www.umo.edu."
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#nursing-faculty": {
      "title": "Nursing Faculty",
      "description": "Nursing Faculty. Department: Nursing. Full-time Faculty. Posted 2026-07-30. The School of Arts & Sciences at the University of Mount Olive seeks applicants for a 12-month, full-time, faculty position to teach Nursing and related coursework. This position will be assigned to the Division of Nursing within the School of Arts & Sciences and will report directly to the Division Chair of Nursing. This in-person faculty position requires a presence on the UMO campus in Mount Olive, NC, and will be responsible for advising, teaching, and supervising majors enrolled in the programs offered within the Division of Nursing, including both our daytime and fast track nighttime Pre-Licensure BSN programs. This position requires some night and weekend teaching assignments. Candidates must be qualified to teach lecture, laboratory and clinical courses. Based on education and professional experience, the faculty member may be assigned additional courses in related disciplines. This is an overview of the duties of this position and not meant to be a comprehensive list. For more information, please contact Professor Donna Larrimore, Chair of the Division of Nursing, at DLarrimore@umo.edu . Minimum Qualifications: · Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from a regionally accredited college or university and nationally accredited MSN program · Hold an active, unencumbered registered nurse (RN) license recognized by the NCBON · Two (2) years of continuous, full-time experience providing direct patient care as a registered nurse within the past five years · Experience utilizing a Learning Management System to create, organize, and deliver course content. · Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills are essential to effectively work with students and faculty. · American Heart Association BLS certification The following qualifications are also preferred: · Doctorate in Nursing or related field (PhD, EdD, or DNP) · Previous teaching experience at the college level is preferred, particularly at an NCBON-approved nursing program · Five (5) years of continuous, full-time experience providing direct patient care as a registered nurse Apply: Send cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, list of three references, and undergraduate and graduate transcripts which must be sent directly from the institutions to: Tammy Williams, Administrative Assistant to the Vice President for Academic Affairs/University of Mount Olive/634 Henderson St/Mount Olive, NC 28365/or email: Facultyapplication@umo.edu"
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#tsb-asst-dean": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean - Tillman School of Business",
      "description": "Assistant Dean - Tillman School of Business. Department: Tillman School of Business. Full-time Staff. Posted 2026-05-15. The University of Mount Olive (UMO), Tillman School of Business (TSB), invites applications for a 12-month, full-time Assistant Dean position. This leadership role provides an opportunity for a highly motivated individual to make a meaningful impact on the lives of traditional and non-traditional adult learners while advancing business programs and processes that support the University’s mission to transform lives through education. The Assistant Dean reports directly to the Dean of the Tillman School of Business and provides leadership in accreditation, assessment, faculty oversight, student advising, student engagement, and academic quality assurance. The position includes teaching responsibilities and close collaboration with faculty and university stakeholders. Responsibilities include: Accreditation, Assessment, and Continuous Improvement Provide leadership and oversight for TSB accreditation activities related to SACSCOC and ACBSP. •Work closely with the Dean, senior leadership, faculty, and institutional stakeholders to ensure compliance and preparation for accreditation reviews. •Guide accreditation vision, goals, strategic plans, and timelines while ensuring accuracy, quality, and timeliness. •Develop and manage assessment processes and procedures supporting continuous improvement of academic programs. •Create and maintain a comprehensive repository of accreditation documentation. •Prepare internal and external reports, executive summaries, and responses to surveys and data requests. Faculty Recruitment, Credentialing, and Evaluation •Chair the hiring committee for all adjunct and full-time faculty positions within the Tillman School of Business. •Lead and coordinate faculty searches in collaboration with Dean and University Human Resources. •Serve as the primary authority for initial faculty credentialing, ensuring compliance with University, SACSCOC, and ACBSP standards. •Maintain faculty qualification and credential documentation. •Conduct performance evaluations for all adjunct faculty. •Participate with the Dean in performance reviews of full-time faculty. Student Advising and Support •Guide and review faculty advising practices to ensure consistent, high-quality advising for business students. •Serve as primary academic advisor for 15–20 undergraduate business students. •Address undergraduate academic and behavioral issues and manage student complaints. •Communicate on academic matters including scheduling, substitutions, directed studies, experiential learning credit, and transfer policy. •Maintain accurate records in accordance with FERPA. Academic Operations and Quality Assurance •Ensure course materials and resources listed in LMS syllabi align with adopted materials available through the University bookstore. •Review and analyze student course evaluation data and use findings to support instructional and content improvement. •Ensure quality and consistency of Adult and Graduate Program Universal Design Templates. •Organize class schedules per advising guides and staff accordingly. Student Engagement and Applied Learning •Work collaboratively with the Director of the UMO Business and Financial Solutions Center to promote applied learning opportunities to business students. •Ensure students interested in the UMO Solutions Center clearly understand program opportunities, responsibilities, and accountability expectations. •Support alignment between academic coursework and experiential learning initiatives. Engagement and Outreach •Assist with admissions, orientation, graduation, and other university- and school-related events. •Collaborate with the Dean and Office of Marketing Communications on recruitment and outreach strategies. Teaching • Teach the equivalent of two courses per semester in an academically qualified discipline within the Tillman School of Business. Minimum Qualifications •Master of Business Administration (MBA) from a regionally accredited institution. Preferred Qualifications •Experience with the ACBSP accreditation process. •Significant industry or professional experience. Compensation and Rank Salary and academic rank are commensurate with education and experience. The University offers a comprehensive benefits package. The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship. To Apply: Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, list of three professional references, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts. Submit to: Manager of Faculty Records University of Mount Olive 634 Henderson Street Mount Olive, NC 28365 or email: facultyapplication@umo.edu The University of Mount Olive is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes applicants from underrepresented groups. To learn more about the University of Mount Olive, please visit: www.umo.edu."
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#psychology-faculty": {
      "title": "Psychology Faculty",
      "description": "Psychology Faculty. Department: School of Arts & Sciences. Full-time Faculty. Posted 2026-04-30. The School of Arts & Sciences at the University of Mount Olive seeks applicants for a 9.5-month, full-time, faculty position to teach Psychology and/or related coursework. Administrative release time will be provided for Graduate program exploration. These duties will include assessing the demand for various Psychology and related graduate programming, making recommendations on such programming to the Faculty and Administration, and subsequently building/designing the curriculum for newly approved graduate programming. This position will be assigned to the Division of Sport and Social Sciences within the School of Arts & Sciences and will report directly to the Assistant Dean of the Division. This in-person faculty position requires a presence on the UMO campus in Mount Olive, NC, and will be responsible for advising, teaching, and supervising students enrolled in our Psychology programs. Teaching assignments may include undergraduate and/or graduate courses and may range from in-person to online and hybrid formats. This faculty member must be qualified to teach graduate and undergraduate courses in Psychology or related field. Based on education and professional experience, the faculty member may be assigned additional courses in related disciplines. For more information, please contact Dr. Jill Mills, Assistant Dean for the Division of Sport and Social Sciences, at JMills@umo.edu Minimum Qualifications: •Doctorate in Psychology or closely related field •Experience utilizing a Learning Management System to create, organize, and deliver course content. •Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills, essential to effectively working with students and faculty. Qualifications Preferred: •Previous experience designing, directing, and developing curriculum for graduate-level programs in Psychology and/or related disciplines •Clinical Psychology background/teaching experience •Previous teaching experience at the collegiate level, especially experience teaching in a graduate program The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship. To Apply: Send cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, list of three references, and undergraduate and graduate transcripts which must be sent directly from the institutions to: Tammy Williams, Administrative Assistant to the Vice President for Academic Affairs/University of Mount Olive/634 Henderson St/Mount Olive, NC 28365. The University of Mount Olive is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes applicants from underrepresented groups. To learn more about the University of Mount Olive, please visit: www.umo.edu."
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#finance-faculty": {
      "title": "Finance – Faculty",
      "description": "Finance – Faculty. Department: Tillman School of Business. Full-time Faculty. Posted 2026-06-15. Finance – Faculty The University of Mount Olive invites applications for a 9-month, full-time, Finance Faculty position. Finance is one of several areas that compose the business core in TSB. Finance courses are taught in traditional (seated) and online (graduate and undergraduate) formats. Responsibilities include: Preference will be given to applicants who have qualifications that enable them to teach in areas of finance and experience, and/or certifications that allow application of data analytics and problem-solving skills in those areas. The ideal candidate will be interested in applying what he/she teach as well as research. Responsibilities include teaching a combination of undergraduate and graduate MBA courses in finance and related subject areas, five courses in fall and spring semesters, respectively. Faculty are required to be contributing members of the department, school, and university. Minimum Qualifications: Master of Finance or other Master's degree with 18 hours in finance Degree(s) must be from regionally accredited institutions Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. or DBA in finance or related field. Industry/professional experience strongly preferred. Compensation and Academic Rank: Commensurate with education and experience. UMO offers a competitive fringe benefit program, including health, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship. To Apply: Send cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, list of three references, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts to: Manager of Faculty Records/University of Mount Olive/634 Henderson St/Mount Olive, NC 28365/or email: facultyapplication@umo.edu . University of Mount Olive is a private institution rooted in the liberal arts with a Christian values, multiple locations, and sponsored by the Convention of Original Free Will Baptists. The University exists to provide an integrated academic experience consisting of quality educational programs, a supportive learning environment, and individual growth opportunities that promote the total development of its students intellectually, socially, and spiritually. The University of Mount Olive is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes applicants from underrepresented groups."
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#nursing-simulation-laboratory-coordinator": {
      "title": "Nursing Simulation Laboratory Coordinator",
      "description": "Nursing Simulation Laboratory Coordinator. Department: School of Arts & Sciences. Full-time Faculty. Posted 2026-07-29. The School of Arts & Sciences at the University of Mount Olive seeks applicants for the position of Nursing Simulation Laboratory Coordinator, a 12-month, full-time, faculty position. The position will require teaching courses in Nursing and related coursework. Administrative release time will be provided for duties related to the maintenance and coordination of the Nursing Simulation Laboratory. This position will be assigned to the Division of Nursing within the School of Arts & Sciences and will report directly to the Division Chair of Nursing. This in-person faculty position requires a presence on the UMO campus in Mount Olive, NC, and will be responsible for advising, teaching, and supervising majors enrolled in the programs offered within the Division of Nursing, including both our daytime and fast-track nighttime Pre-Licensure BSN programs. This position requires some night and weekend teaching assignments. The position will also require coordination of the Nursing Simulation Laboratory, which may include one-on-one and/or group lab and simulation instruction. Candidates must be qualified to teach lecture, laboratory and clinical courses. Based on education and professional experience, the faculty member may be assigned additional courses in related disciplines. This is an overview of the duties of this position and not meant to be a comprehensive list. For more information, please contact Professor Donna Larrimore, Chair of the Division of Nursing, at DLarrimore@umo.edu . Minimum Qualifications: · Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from a regionally accredited college or university and nationally accredited MSN program · Hold an active, unencumbered registered nurse (RN) license recognized by the NCBON · Two (2) years of continuous, full-time experience providing direct patient care as a registered nurse within the past five years · Experience utilizing a Learning Management System to create, organize, and deliver course content · Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills, essential to effectively working with students and co-workers · American Heart Association BLS certification The following qualifications are also preferred: · Doctorate in Nursing or related field (PhD, EdD, or DNP) · Previous teaching experience at the collegiate level, particularly at an NCBON-approved Nursing program · Five (5) or more years of continuous, full-time experience providing direct patient care as a registered nurse · Experience with clinical facilitation of student learning within the last five years · Priority will be given to applicants who have knowledge, skills, and experience utilizing high fidelity simulators and other equipment, technology, and software used within the Nursing Simulation Laboratory The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship. Apply: Send cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, list of three references, and undergraduate and graduate transcripts which must be sent directly from the institutions to: Tammy Williams, Administrative Assistant to the Vice President for Academic Affairs/University of Mount Olive/634 Henderson St/Mount Olive, NC 28365/or email: Facultyapplication@umo.edu"
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#student-conduct-coordinator": {
      "title": "Student Conduct Coordinator",
      "description": "Student Conduct Coordinator. Department: Student Affairs. Full-time Staff. Posted 2026-07-29. The Student Conduct Coordinator is a full-time, twelve-month live-in position that will be responsible for managing the university’s student conduct process. This position will serve as the student conduct administrator, ensuring compliance with all university policies and processes as well as the protection of student responsibilities and rights. This administrator will oversee the adjudication of all conduct hearings, processes, and notifications. This component of the position will require a professional who is detail-oriented and can manage multiple tasks simultaneously. In addition to the student conduct component, this administrator will oversee a residential area of two residence halls (approximately 200 students) and supervise five to eight resident assistants. Responsibilities will include staff training, conflict mediation, crisis intervention, and the implementation of residence hall programming designed to complement the goals of the residence life program and the mission of the university. This live-in position will require flexible hours, a team-building attitude, and a sincere desire to work with students in a religiously affiliated private liberal arts college environment. This position will serve as the administrator for two residential facilities on campus. This position will work closely with two other assistant director professionals to coordinate all housing and residence life functions. We anticipate additional professional opportunities based on the operational needs and programming interests of our faculty, staff, and students. This position will be an excellent opportunity for a motivated professional seeking a broad student affairs experience in a small private college environment. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree preferred. Supervisory experience and extensive experience in residential living, either as a graduate student or full-time employee, are required. Also, experience working with a college judicial system is preferred. Salary is competitive, full college benefits, semi-furnished apartment, and a meal plan provided. The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship. For consideration, submit a resume and a list of references to Dr. Dan Sullivan, Senior Vice President for Student Affairs at dsullivan@umo.edu . Accepting applications until position is filled. University of Mount Olive is an EEO employer."
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#business-management-faculty": {
      "title": "Business Management Faculty",
      "description": "Business Management Faculty. Department: Tillman School of Business. Full-time Faculty. Posted 2026-08-14. Business Management The University of Mount Olive, Tillman School of Business (TSB), invites applications for a 9.5-month, full-time Management Faculty position. The Tillman School of Business undergraduate programs are accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP). TSB’s Bachelor of Science in Business Administration (BSBA) curriculum includes a comprehensive business core, requiring all majors to complete foundational management courses such as Management Principles, Human Capital Management, Management Information Systems, Marketing Management, and International Business Management. Students pursuing the Management concentration complete 30 semester hours that include Business Communications, Total Quality Management and Analytics, Business Policy and Strategy, Organizational Behavior, Operations and Supply Chain Management, Entrepreneurship and Small Business Management, and Project Management. UMO also offers the Master of Business Administration, with concentrations in Accounting and Healthcare Management. Courses are delivered in multiple formats, including daytime seated, online undergraduate, and online graduate instruction. Minimum Qualifications Minimum of five years of applied business experience MBA or Master of Science in a management discipline Other master’s degree specifically related to business Degree(s) must be earned from regionally accredited institutions Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. or DBA in management or a closely related field 10+ years of industry or professional experience The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship. To Apply: Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, list of three references, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts to the VPAA, University of Mount Olive, 634 Henderson St, Mount Olive, NC 28365, or email facultyapplication@umo.edu . The University of Mount Olive is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes applicants from underrepresented groups."
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#slate-crm-administrator": {
      "title": "Slate CRM Administrator",
      "description": "Slate CRM Administrator. Department: Institutional Research & Planning. Full-time Staff. Posted 2026-10-01. The University of Mount Olive has an immediate opening for a Slate CRM Administrator. Responsibilities include: Lead Slate CRM administration, collaborating with institutional stakeholders to effectively use the system to meet enrollment, student success, and retention goals. Build and maintain system configurations, integrations, communications, forms, queries, reports, workflows, and portals. Analyze complex business problems and design solutions that ensure user needs are addressed comprehensively and effectively. Manage Slate user access and CRM user permissions. Assist users, resolving technical issues and providing education as needed. Monitor and ensure data accuracy and integrity for system use as well as institutional policy, accreditation and regulatory compliance. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required, Advanced degree preferred. Must have three years' Slate CRM as well as three years of professional experience working with higher education. The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship. The University of Mount Olive is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body and welcomes applicants from underrepresented groups. To learn more about the University of Mount Olive, please visit www.umo.edu."
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#title-iii-coordinator": {
      "title": "Title III Coordinator",
      "description": "Title III Coordinator. Department: Title III. Full-time Staff. Posted 2026-10-05. Title III Coordinator — Grant Funded Position The University of Mount Olive seeks a full-time Title III Coordinator. This position is grant-funded for the duration of the grant. Primary duties include directing, managing, and overseeing UMO Title III project activities on behalf of the Title III Director to ensure timely achievement of goals and objectives, effective use of resources, and full compliance with Title III, U.S. DoL, and UMO policies and procedures; develop and approve budgetary expenditures; allocate human, material, and fiscal resources to the programs and related activities; maintain equipment inventories; draft fiscal, technical, and progress reports for all constituencies; measure project performance and recommend corrective action when necessary to respective supervision; guide institutionalization; and help ensure long-term continuation. For more information, please contact Burt Lewis, Vice-President, Academic Affairs, blewis@umo.edu . Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in education or related field Previous teaching or management experience Knowledge of campus operations/relationships Experience with strategies for improving student retention and experience Team oriented Project leader Attention to detail The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship."
    },
    "https://umo.edu/employment/#instructional-designer": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer",
      "description": "Instructional Designer. Department: Teaching Excellence Center. Full-time Staff. Posted 2026-10-14. The University of Mount Olive invites applications for a full-time Instructional Designer within the Teaching Excellence Center, beginning in January 2027. The Instructional Designer works collaboratively with faculty to support high-quality instruction across modalities, with particular emphasis on the integration of artificial intelligence into teaching and learning. Established with support from a federal Title III grant, this position is well suited for an early-career instructional designer seeking to grow their experience while contributing to University-wide initiatives in instructional design, faculty development, artificial intelligence, and educational technology. This is a campus-based position at the University of Mount Olive. Occasional evening and weekend work and travel may be required. Responsibilities include: The Instructional Designer will: Collaborate with faculty to design, develop, and enhance online, hybrid, and technology-enhanced courses. Support the development and implementation of the University’s AI literacy framework and AI-related academic programming, including the integration of AI across general education and discipline-specific curricula. Develop and deliver faculty professional development related to instructional design, AI-enhanced teaching, responsible use of AI, and emerging educational technologies. Support faculty AI learning communities and other opportunities for collaboration and peer learning. Research, pilot, and evaluate educational technologies and AI tools for instructional use. Develop and maintain Moodle courses and instructional resources using learner-centered and adult-learning principles. Conduct course readiness and quality reviews using University expectations and established standards, including Quality Matters, Universal Design for Learning, digital accessibility, and regular and substantive interaction. Provide faculty consultations, coaching, workshops, and other instructional design support. Develop faculty development resources, courses, tutorials, guides, and other materials. Support Title III and other University initiatives related to instructional design, artificial intelligence, faculty development, and educational technology. Maintain appropriate documentation to support assessment, accreditation, grant reporting, and continuous improvement. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Instructional Design, Educational Technology, Curriculum and Instruction, Learning Sciences, Education, or a closely related field. Minimum of two years of relevant instructional design experience. Knowledge of instructional design principles, adult learning, course design, assessment, and effective teaching practices. Experience with learning management systems and instructional technologies. Knowledge of generative AI and its applications in teaching and learning. Working knowledge of Universal Design for Learning, digital accessibility practices, and WCAG guidelines. Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, project management, and organizational skills. Current Quality Matters credentials or willingness to complete the University-designated Quality Matters professional development pathway within six months of hire and maintain required credentials thereafter. Experience in higher education and/or adult learning environments is preferred. Experience with Moodle, Articulate 360, Rise 360, Camtasia, Microsoft Teams, or comparable technologies is also preferred. To Apply: Interested applicants should submit the following to Tammy Williams at twilliams@umo.edu : Letter of interest Resume Contact information for three professional references, including at least one current or former supervisor One to three examples of work demonstrating experience in instructional design, faculty development, or educational technology. Links, screenshots, or redacted samples are acceptable; a formal portfolio is not required. The University of Mount Olive requires candidates to be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring current or future visa sponsorship."
    },
